I go back to the customer service desk.
The shop assistant is already waiting.
"Is this shirt better than the other one?" she asks.
"Yes, much better," I answer.
"The size is exactly right."
She smiles warmly.
"Wonderful, then I will exchange that now," she says.
She types quickly on her computer.
Then she gives me the shirt and the new till receipt.
I take my things.
Carefully, I pack the shirt into the backpack.
"I wish you a nice weekend!" the shop assistant says.
"Thank you, I wish you the same!" I answer.
I walk out of the shop.
The afternoon in May is wonderfully warm.
Now I am finally ready for the Berlin summer.
